OHOS: run the daemon manager against the host through the desktop bridge. The
app sandbox can neither run the CLI nor see ~/.multica, so file and CLI access
go through ohos-host; health and API calls use net.fetch, because the global
fetch needs WebAssembly, which is missing; the log panel polls by offset; a
missing CLI is retried every 5 s; and once the CLI recovers the daemon is
started for a user who has signed in, since the renderer's login sync cannot
reach auto-start while the bridge is down.

